{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_page", "label": "User-defined type guards", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "label": "Type predicate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A return type of the form x is T lets narrowing survive a function call. A plain boolean return narrows nothing. Reuses one check everywhere and works with filter/find, but the compiler takes your word for the body."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_unverified_body", "label": "Compiler does not check guard body", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "function isCat(p): p is Cat { return true } compiles. A predicate is an assertion in function form \u2014 written once and trusted at every call site, so a wrong one is more expensive than a wrong as."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_isdefined", "label": "isDefined filter guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "filter(v => v != null) keeps (T | null)[] because the arrow is not a type predicate. A named isDefined<T>(v): v is T lets filter narrow to T[]."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_iskeyof", "label": "isKeyOf type predicate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only way to convince the compiler a string is a valid key: k is keyof T. The in operator narrows the object, never the key."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_schema_validator", "label": "Schema validator over hand-written guards", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guards for small structural checks. A validator (zod, valibot) for anything crossing a boundary: it performs the runtime check and derives the type from one declaration."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_page", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_unverified_body", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_isdefined", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_iskeyof", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_narrows_object_not_key", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_schema_validator", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_page", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_04_instanceof_narrowing_structural_iserror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_schema_validator", "target": "docs_typescript_syllabus_03_in_the_stack_schema_first", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "target": "docs_typescript_syllabus_03_in_the_stack_parse_dont_validate", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/07-type-guards.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "boundary_unknown_to_domain", "label": "Turning unknown into a domain type", "nodes": ["docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_07_type_guards_type_predicate", "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrow